WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.080
"Get these dinosaurs out of here!" cried Professor Flashback.

2
00:00:09.081 --> 00:00:13.556
Several dinosaurs jumped onto a table and knocked over equipment.

3
00:00:13.557 --> 00:00:16.416
A small clock fell down and broke.

4
00:00:16.417 --> 00:00:19.705
Another dinosaur ate books from the bookshelf.

5
00:00:19.706 --> 00:00:22.692
"They're destroying my laboratory!"

6
00:00:22.693 --> 00:00:25.393
Professor Flashback pulled at his hair.

7
00:00:25.394 --> 00:00:28.732
Roxy saw a big dinosaur bump into the big clock.

8
00:00:28.733 --> 00:00:30.725
The clock rocked.

9
00:00:30.726 --> 00:00:32.453
Roxy gulped.

10
00:00:32.454 --> 00:00:37.407
"If that clock breaks, Metro City will be trapped in the past!"

11
00:00:37.408 --> 00:00:39.944
She darted to the clock and grabbed it.

12
00:00:39.945 --> 00:00:45.497
The clock's big hand was pointing to the year 65 million BC.

13
00:00:45.498 --> 00:00:48.443
"Shoo!" said Professor Flashback.

14
00:00:48.444 --> 00:00:51.970
He was pushing three small dinosaurs away with a broom.

15
00:00:51.971 --> 00:00:54.875
He suddenly spotted Roxy near the clock.

16
00:00:54.876 --> 00:00:57.529
"What are you doing?" he yelled.

17
00:00:57.530 --> 00:00:59.039
Roxy glared at him.

18
00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:02.687
"I'm bringing Metro City back to the present!"

19
00:01:02.688 --> 00:01:04.982
She grabbed the clock's hand.

20
00:01:04.983 --> 00:01:10.091
"No!" cried Professor Flashback. "Do not—oof!"

21
00:01:10.092 --> 00:01:12.980
A fat dinosaur knocked the professor down.

22
00:01:12.981 --> 00:01:15.377
Roxy yanked the clock's hand.

23
00:01:15.378 --> 00:01:22.508
She turned it to the present.

24
00:01:22.509 --> 00:01:27.393
Electricity shot through the lab.

25
00:01:27.394 --> 00:01:30.491
In a moment the electricity was gone.

26
00:01:30.492 --> 00:01:32.776
And so were the dinosaurs.

27
00:01:32.777 --> 00:01:36.883
Roxy took a deep breath. "Whew!"

28
00:01:36.884 --> 00:01:39.242
Professor Flashback grinned.

29
00:01:39.243 --> 00:01:41.903
"Thanks for saving my clock," he said.

30
00:01:41.904 --> 00:01:44.185
Roxy turned back to the clock.

31
00:01:44.186 --> 00:01:49.593
Whiz-hoo! Her eye laser beams blew the clock into a million pieces. "No!"

32
00:01:49.594 --> 00:01:53.541
the professor cried. "That

33
00:01:53.542 --> 00:01:56.642
clock is dangerous," said Roxy. "And

34
00:01:56.643 --> 00:02:00.808
you, Professor Flashback, are in big trouble." The

35
00:02:00.809 --> 00:02:03.522
professor narrowed his eyes at Roxy. He

36
00:02:03.523 --> 00:02:05.481
pulled his sleeve up. A

37
00:02:05.482 --> 00:02:08.449
small golden watch was on his wrist. "Good-bye,

38
00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:12.158
Rocket Girl," said Professor Flashback. He

39
00:02:12.159 --> 00:02:15.166
pressed a button on his watch. Za-wap!

40
00:02:15.167 --> 00:02:20.236
Electricity flashed and the professor disappeared! Roxy

41
00:02:20.237 --> 00:02:22.261
scratched her head. "I

42
00:02:22.262 --> 00:02:25.460
wonder where he went." The

43
00:02:25.461 --> 00:02:29.415
next day Roxy and her friends were at the Natural History Museum. Lots

44
00:02:29.416 --> 00:02:32.634
of fossils and dinosaur bones were on display. "Wow!"

45
00:02:32.635 --> 00:02:39.683
said Jack. "A T. rex skeleton!" Mara

46
00:02:39.684 --> 00:02:45.341
smiled. "It's a lot less scary than a live T. rex." Roxy

47
00:02:45.342 --> 00:02:47.658
pretended to sigh. "I

48
00:02:47.659 --> 00:02:51.634
can't believe I missed those dinosaurs." Terrell

49
00:02:51.635 --> 00:02:56.682
gave her a suspicious look. The

50
00:02:56.683 --> 00:03:00.074
friends saw a cave painting from the Stone Age. It

51
00:03:00.075 --> 00:03:02.594
showed cavemen hunting animals. One

52
00:03:02.595 --> 00:03:05.822
caveman looked different from the others. "Is

53
00:03:05.823 --> 00:03:09.176
that guy wearing a hat ?" asked Terrell.

54
00:03:09.177 --> 00:03:11.551
"I think so," said Jack.

55
00:03:11.552 --> 00:03:14.967
"It looks like he has binoculars too."

56
00:03:14.968 --> 00:03:17.532
"That's weird," said Mara.

57
00:03:17.533 --> 00:03:20.573
"Binoculars didn't exist back then!"

58
00:03:20.574 --> 00:03:25.880
Roxy looked at the man and smiled.

59
00:03:25.881 --> 00:03:31.848
But she didn't say a word to her friends.

